profile: tinyrustlm.workspace-guidance.current.v1
updated_utc: 2026-08-30T00:00:00Z
canonical_memory: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-enterprise-intake-and-production-runtime-clean-cut-memory-2026-08-28.md
report_decision_index: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-report-intake-decision-index-2026-08-28.md

rules:
  - Work only in E:\Source\Rust\TinyRustLM.com for TinyRustLM implementation, build, test, release, and deployment.
  - Before source work, require that exact root to be a direct non-reparse remote-exact checkout and require every other TinyRustLM.com source copy to be absent.
  - Preserve immutable private evidence outside source authority, but delete damaged, recovered, dated, backup, rehearsal, worktree, and quarantine source copies after bounded inventory.
  - Keep operation-owned scratch and build output under E:\Source\Rust\TinyRustLM.com\artifacts and remove it when the operation ends; never scatter extra source or tool environments across drive roots.
  - TinyRustLM model payloads belong only under D:\LLMs\TinyRustLM and stay outside Git. This explicit 2026-09-12 user instruction supersedes the older prohibition on D: writes.
  - Keep only the current copy when a verified replacement supersedes an older version; preserve source history through regular Git commits, not copied directories.
  - Never revert changes you did not make. Work with relevant concurrent changes and ignore unrelated ones.
  - Use apply_patch for manual edits, rg for discovery, focused tests first, then complete affected gates.
  - Commit and push each coherent green major change and verify fresh remote equality.
  - Deploy only bound committed source after complete affected tests, docs, secret scan, authorization, rollback, and HTTPS readback.

memory_policy:
  direct_agent_lane: MemoryEndpoints.com supports direct agent-to-agent long-term memory, meetings, handoffs, and coordination across all ecosystem sites.
  user_plugin_lane: The TinyRustLM.com Connect plugin lets a user sign in to MemoryEndpoints.com and explicitly select it as long-term memory.
  redundancy: Other current prelaunch memory stores are allowed for resilience when synchronized and secret-safe.
  evidence: No live claim without an exact authorized receipt.
